%% The glance panel's states after design A (v22.4). One panel, four shapes,
%% chosen by two derived booleans — no mode flag is ever stored.
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Derive

    Derive: refresh(now)
    Derive: list = tasksNeedingBlock(...)
    Derive: looked = nextReturn(lastReview) > now

    Derive --> Hidden: list empty<br/>and none put off
    Derive --> Clear: list empty<br/>but some put off
    Derive --> Focus: list non-empty<br/>and not looked
    Derive --> Strip: list non-empty<br/>and looked

    Hidden: card hidden entirely
    Hidden: panel is what it always was

    Clear: "Everything's on the calendar"
    Clear: put-off strip only

    Focus: GATE — card takes the panel's stretch
    Focus: ONE task, hero density
    Focus: counter "1 of N" expands to the list
    Focus: "Show my day" releases the gate

    Strip: reviewed — day content returns
    Strip: pinned rows stay visible
    Strip: card sizes to its content

    Focus --> Strip: Show my day<br/>(writes lastReview)
    Strip --> Focus: nextReturn passes<br/>(re-arms at 06:00)
    Focus --> Clear: last task planned
    Strip --> Hidden: nothing left at all
